

------BP ANNOTATION------
MAIN LOGIC

Each bp = bnd1(CHROM1, POS1, orientation1) + insert + bnd2(CHROM2, POS2, orientation2)

1. DEL if same chrom, N[...]N, POS2 - POS1 > len(insert)
2. INS if same chrom, N[...]N, POS2 - POS1 <= len(insert)
3. DUP if same chrom, ]N...N[, POS2 - POS1 >= 0
4. INV if same chrom, either N]...N] or [N...[N
5. Look at what remains, decide then. Should be inter-chrom stuff


------DATA NOTES------
Currently filtering by svlen is only available for DELs, INSs and DUPs. All other vars have svlen 1

Notes on datasets:
HG00514:
    - 30x coverage

Notes on val sets:
Huddleston2016 for CHM13 (huddleston):
    - >=50 SVLEN
    - 20516 bps
    - DEL,INS,INV
GIAB for HG002 (hg002_val):
    - min len - 20bp
    - 89995 bps
    - DEL,INS
Kosugi for NA12878 (kosugi):
    - >50 SVLEN
    - 24089 bps
    - DEL,INS,DUP,INV


